1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,700
Stand up tall, reach out your hand.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,880
Cut through the wind and make a stand.

3
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:11,220
The paint within brings
out a map of your own.

4
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:19,680
To the left and the right,
all we saw stormy nights.

5
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:22,960
All the rough winds and
waves coming day after day.

6
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:26,180
And the values we had
were about to collapse.

7
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:28,777
Oh, just where do we go next?

8
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:35,440
And as we look down to the compass in
hand Is it showing us the right direction?

9
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:38,637
All we know is nobody
here knows it for certain.

10
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:41,957
So close your eyes and breathe in deeply.

11
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:45,157
And listen to your soul.

12
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:48,117
You'll see a path in front of you.

13
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,537
And you'll know just where you need to go.

14
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:55,817
So stand up tall, reach out your hand.

15
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,037
Cut through the wind and make us stand.

16
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:02,900
Don't let the darkness
win, just break through.

17
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:08,137
I'll do it my own way,
that's what's best for me.

18
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:11,797
And you do it your way,
that's how it's got to be.

19
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:15,357
We're moving forward, now I'm ready.

20
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:19,217
But at times it's okay
to get help on the way.

21
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:21,757
For the future ahead, burning bright.

22
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:24,177
For what's ahead you see.

23
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:27,620
Is beyond your wildest dreams.

24
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:31,757
So stand up tall, reach out your hand.

25
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:34,997
Cut through the wind and make a stand.

26
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:38,820
Don't let the darkness
win, just break through.

27
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:44,097
We'll do it our way,
the best that we know.

28
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:45,577
With tears and doubts and tone.

29
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:47,897
We'll go where we all wanna go.

30
00:01:47,980 --> 00:01:52,440
The page within brings colors of our own.

31
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,480
You heard him, didn't you?

32
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,240
Let's keep up the fight!

33
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:51,320
You really believe Straw
Hat will defeat me?

34
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:56,720
You really believe that
Wano's borders will open?

35
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:58,740
Just a fairy tale ending.

36
00:03:00,420 --> 00:03:02,680
You're nothing but a damn child!

37
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:06,640
There's no way I'm losing!

38
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:08,740
I will defeat Kaido!

39
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:12,980
Our samurai are strong!

40
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:14,947
We're not waiting for Luffy!

41
00:03:15,060 --> 00:03:16,531
We're facing you head on!

42
00:03:18,220 --> 00:03:19,050
We're...

43
00:03:19,133 --> 00:03:20,160
Good luck.

44
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,180
You're not alone.

45
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:28,440
I'll die beside you if I must.

46
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:32,539
Fripe Fripe Jutsu!

47
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:54,790
Grr.

48
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:02,240
Robot, Robot.

49
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:05,620
Momonosuke is out!

50
00:04:05,940 --> 00:04:06,940
They're finished.

51
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:09,957
The samurai don't have a leader
anymore if that Brad's dead.

52
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:12,537
We gotta broadcast his
death to the whole island.

53
00:04:12,620 --> 00:04:14,437
They'll surrender, of course, of course.

54
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:15,991
They've got nothing left.

55
00:04:16,220 --> 00:04:18,120
Oh, that's a great idea!

56
00:04:18,380 --> 00:04:20,257
Let's crush their spirits!

57
00:04:20,340 --> 00:04:21,640
She's alive!

58
00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:23,660
The crow is coming back!

59
00:04:24,220 --> 00:04:27,097
Let's make our way to the performance
floor just like we planned.

60
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:28,360
Sound good? Uh-huh.

61
00:04:28,620 --> 00:04:32,420
If Loopy is doing his best,
then we will as well. Agreed.

62
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:34,720
I'm so happy for Straw Hat.

63
00:04:35,380 --> 00:04:36,210
Huh?

64
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:39,240
Is my Climatac talking to me?

65
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:41,860
Hello, Nami. No way.

66
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:43,880
It has a face too?

67
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:46,960
This is weird! Jeepers!

68
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:49,120
It's so cute!

69
00:04:50,340 --> 00:04:52,340
Ma-ma-ma-ma-ha!

70
00:04:52,780 --> 00:04:55,486
You really think Straw
Hat could defeat Kaido?

71
00:04:55,620 --> 00:04:57,900
Are you stupid, or is this some joke?

72
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:01,637
I was just hoping I'd have the
pleasure of killing him myself.

73
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:02,680
But it's fine.

74
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:06,527
As long as he's dead, at least
he won't be a thorn in my side.

75
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:14,457
Speaking as someone who's
worked with him for a while,

76
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:18,800
I have a feeling he'll survive, even
if it doesn't make any damn sense.

77
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:19,857
Who asked you?

78
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:21,477
This is my fight.

79
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:23,337
Big mom's the enemy here.

80
00:05:23,420 --> 00:05:26,500
Our enemy, so grow up!

81
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:33,320
This once we can form an alliance.

82
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:44,637
Maybe I'm such a genius that my
genius even surpassed myself.

83
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:47,057
Huh, I made that thing.

84
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:52,040
So if it can talk, it must be my
doing. What? No! Look, it's me!

85
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:53,380
You're all buzzers!

86
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:56,540
Last I saw, that other cloud ate you!

87
00:05:56,820 --> 00:05:59,055
How the heck did you end up like this?

88
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:00,620
That was weird.

89
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:05,100
After Mama grabbed me, my
spirit started leaving my body.

90
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:07,600
Finish him off, Hera!

91
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:13,080
I was lost in a daze. Powerless.

92
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:16,260
And that Lady Hera was gonna couple me up!

93
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:20,800
I'll give you a snack out of pity.

94
00:06:21,300 --> 00:06:23,280
Eat them and run, okay, girl?

95
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:25,850
Hurry!

96
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:29,932
Then you stretched out your
weapon and offered me a snack.

97
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:31,920
Eat them! Come on!

98
00:06:32,380 --> 00:06:33,400
Wake up!

99
00:06:34,100 --> 00:06:35,400
Here I go!

100
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:37,369
It's dinner time for more.

101
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:42,893
Anyhow, I guess when Hera bit me, it
smushed my body into your rod thingy.

102
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:45,257
And just like magic...

103
00:06:45,340 --> 00:06:47,740
I came back to life, good as new.

104
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:52,327
Well, that's fine for you, but
it's a pain in the butt for me.

105
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:53,750
Oh, wait.

106
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:57,076
Even though you saved me,
you haven't forgiven me yet?

107
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,080
I don't have so much power anymore.

108
00:07:01,460 --> 00:07:03,297
If you could just find
it in your heart, too.

109
00:07:03,380 --> 00:07:04,620
Hold on, hold on.

110
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:09,610
Oh, hey.

111
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:11,217
That looks like the stage.

112
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:13,557
Tama, let's go there and give a command.

113
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:14,470
Right.

114
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:17,160
You listening, Onigashima?

115
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:18,760
I've got news!

116
00:07:19,360 --> 00:07:21,500
The enemy's leader, Momo!

117
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:24,973
I'm sorry to interrupt, ma
'am, but the Sawhats are here!

118
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:27,360
It's a Huang lat!

119
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:28,760
Huang motor!

120
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:31,510
Listen!

121
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:37,040
I get it now.

122
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:40,060
This brat is the real problem! Tama!

123
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:45,157
Because of her, our gifters started
betraying each other one after the other.

124
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:49,120
She even got Big Mom on her side. No way.

125
00:07:49,340 --> 00:07:52,634
She took that attack from Big
Mom and got right back up?

126
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:55,560
Papa got beat up because of you.

127
00:07:56,180 --> 00:07:58,533
I thought I told you to leave her alone.

128
00:08:03,380 --> 00:08:04,210
What?

129
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:07,697
I've never seen it do that before.

130
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:10,486
Mommy, just use your
baton like you always do.

131
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:12,268
I'll add attacks of my own.

132
00:08:12,660 --> 00:08:14,837
Your skin's too tough
for us to break through.

133
00:08:14,920 --> 00:08:18,273
Instead, we'll damage our
insides like Mama's attack did.

134
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:23,037
One good lightning blast
should do the trick.

135
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:25,414
No, that'll cause too much destruction.

136
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:31,300
We have to keep Otama sick.

137
00:08:33,860 --> 00:08:34,780
What, Capote?

138
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:37,240
You got this, pal?

139
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:41,180
They're so dead!

140
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:44,400
Special attack, green star!

141
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:45,910
Sir Koza!

142
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:49,640
I separated them! Let me go!

143
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:50,820
I'm on it!

144
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:57,440
I thought Luffy's defeat
would shut the samurai down,

145
00:08:57,700 --> 00:09:00,112
but not a single one of them surrendered.

146
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:05,717
Allow me to brief you on the situation.

147
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:11,140
A total of 5,000 troops on both sides
have been rendered unfit for combat.

148
00:09:11,540 --> 00:09:12,834
When the battle began,

149
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:17,780
the Beast Pirates had 24,000
fighters, and the Rebels had 3,000.

150
00:09:20,380 --> 00:09:21,210
However,

151
00:09:21,293 --> 00:09:23,457
all of the pleasures and
waiters on the performance

152
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:26,305
floor seem to have turned
against Master Queen.

153
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:29,660
So the enemy gained 4,000 recruits.

154
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:34,320
At present, the Beast Pirates
have roughly 20,000 troops,

155
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:36,960
and the Rebels have roughly 7,000.

156
00:09:37,340 --> 00:09:41,320
I didn't expect to see the gap
begin to close so late in the game.

157
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:45,020
The situation is completely volatile.

158
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:50,344
On that note, we just received a report
that might cause another shift in balance.

159
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:54,340
It's the Gifters!

160
00:09:54,620 --> 00:09:55,997
They came here to kill us!

161
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:57,200
You're so screwed!

162
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:00,300
Pack it up, you traitors!

163
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:01,755
The gifters are here!

164
00:10:02,360 --> 00:10:06,217
So the pleasures and waiters on this
floor revolted against Master Queen?

165
00:10:06,300 --> 00:10:08,117
What, do they have a death wish?

166
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:10,024
Yeah, not very smart, are they?

167
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:11,180
Don't they get it?

168
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:15,280
Those peons are supposed to be
sacrificed at times like this.

169
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:18,620
Trash has no right to complain
about being taken out.

170
00:10:18,760 --> 00:10:20,777
Wipe out every traitor on the floor!

171
00:10:20,860 --> 00:10:21,980
Show no mercy!

172
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:26,910
Ah!

173
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:30,240
Gorilla Punch Punch!

174
00:10:30,540 --> 00:10:31,440
Suck on that!

175
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:35,880
Rutheran Zeus!

176
00:10:36,580 --> 00:10:38,220
Thundercloud, you're up!

177
00:10:43,660 --> 00:10:44,490
Hello?

178
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:46,700
Zeus, you're out!

179
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:48,410
Huh?

180
00:10:48,493 --> 00:10:50,880
I don't know if I'd call
me Zeus anymore. Huh?

181
00:10:51,200 --> 00:10:55,700
I'm a cool new me after all, So why
don't you give me a cool new name?

182
00:10:57,300 --> 00:10:58,130
Uh...

183
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,180
What is it?

184
00:11:00,380 --> 00:11:01,360
What is it?

185
00:11:01,540 --> 00:11:02,820
Tell me, tell me!

186
00:11:04,280 --> 00:11:05,600
Okay! Yes?

187
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:07,760
You're Fluff!

188
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:13,955
I'll stick with Zeus!

189
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:18,520
If you want to get to Nami,
you gotta go through me!

190
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:20,153
Give it your best shot!

191
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:23,840
I'm so sick of you!

192
00:11:24,680 --> 00:11:25,960
Yeah? Same.

193
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:29,214
We've been playing tag for long enough.

194
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:31,660
I'm putting an end to this right now!

195
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:35,430
Lightning!

196
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:37,670
Lightning!

197
00:11:48,840 --> 00:11:49,760
Oh no!

198
00:11:49,940 --> 00:11:51,240
It's over.

199
00:11:55,640 --> 00:11:56,920
No, it's not!

200
00:11:57,180 --> 00:11:59,100
It's my job to hit my target!

201
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:01,460
And that's what I'm gonna do!

202
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:29,840
I can't believe this!

203
00:12:30,220 --> 00:12:32,060
That means I need help you!

204
00:12:33,560 --> 00:12:35,900
And what Paige might already do?

205
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:40,520
They've managed to take out
two of them as a dummy so slow!

206
00:12:41,700 --> 00:12:42,530
What?

207
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:44,479
You're kidding me?

208
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:46,997
Are these guys a lot
stronger than we thought?

209
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:48,777
We're not actually losing, are we?

210
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:50,000
No, it can't be!

211
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:51,220
Calm down, Mace.

212
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:54,242
Everyone on Onigashima
can hear you freaking out!

213
00:12:54,480 --> 00:12:55,440
Oh, shoot!

214
00:12:55,660 --> 00:12:57,660
I forgot I was still broadcasting!

215
00:12:58,460 --> 00:12:59,290
Ah!

216
00:12:59,373 --> 00:13:01,320
Um, did I say they beat Lady Oji?

217
00:13:01,540 --> 00:13:03,240
I meant Baby Robin Oji!

218
00:13:03,660 --> 00:13:06,200
So she works as a transmitter, huh?

219
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:08,960
All right, then. Oof!

220
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:11,880
Special Attack Green Star Devil!

221
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:16,590
Ah!

222
00:13:30,420 --> 00:13:31,680
Hey, Tama!

223
00:13:32,620 --> 00:13:36,197
I don't know how her power works,
but that girl is like a transmitter.

224
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:39,456
If you make a command, the
whole island will hear you.

225
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:40,840
Go for it!

226
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:04,760
This is Otama!

227
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:08,500
Is that a kid?

228
00:14:09,860 --> 00:14:10,980
Otama is here?

229
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:12,220
What's she doing?

230
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:14,640
It's not safe for her here. It's her!

231
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:16,300
Go get her, Master!

232
00:14:35,740 --> 00:14:37,740
One more round!

233
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:39,320
One more kiss!

234
00:14:57,580 --> 00:14:59,860
It's beautiful, isn't it, Otokon?

235
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:05,720
The fire festival is our time
to honor those we've lost.

236
00:15:06,020 --> 00:15:08,900
We build a fire to reach
them in heaven itself.

237
00:15:09,920 --> 00:15:12,400
I wonder if Daddy can see it.

238
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:16,380
Yes, of course he can.

239
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:19,460
There isn't a cloud in the sky, after all.

240
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:24,937
I'm sure he's watching
over you and watching

241
00:15:25,020 --> 00:15:27,920
over the fate of this
country he loved so well.

242
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:43,680
You heard a voice?

243
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:49,577
Someone's there what?

244
00:15:49,660 --> 00:15:51,317
You're right I see something.

245
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:52,357
Wait a sec!

246
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:53,620
Is that Straw Hat?

247
00:15:54,460 --> 00:15:56,797
How the hell did you hear him underwater?

248
00:15:56,880 --> 00:15:58,660
Who cares? Just bring him in!

249
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:00,890
Hurry!

250
00:16:00,973 --> 00:16:01,803
He might be alive!

251
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:04,160
Whose baby is that?

252
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:06,341
Get out of here, you little shit!

253
00:16:06,540 --> 00:16:07,834
This is a battlefield!

254
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:10,791
And what the hell did you do to Bao Huang?

255
00:16:11,700 --> 00:16:12,660
Answer me!

256
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:17,510
Utama!

257
00:16:17,593 --> 00:16:18,423
Hang in there!

258
00:16:18,540 --> 00:16:19,380
You got this!

259
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:35,030
Ah!

260
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:38,317
Aren't you gonna complain
about being outnumbered?

261
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:39,576
Seems pretty unfair.

262
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:42,780
It was 5,000 versus
30,000 when we came here.

263
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:46,117
This is what everyone expected
from the very beginning.

264
00:16:46,200 --> 00:16:49,180
A one-on-one battle was
never in the cards for me.

265
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:51,480
How annoyingly pragmatic of you.

266
00:16:51,800 --> 00:16:53,177
This is no fun.

267
00:16:53,260 --> 00:16:56,660
Our job is to keep the top
officers busy till Luffy wins.

268
00:16:56,880 --> 00:16:58,704
So grumble as long as you like.

269
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,680
It's one after another with these guys.

270
00:17:05,460 --> 00:17:08,860
A knock him down and more show up.

271
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:13,320
Strength and determination mean nothing.

272
00:17:14,520 --> 00:17:16,700
You know what matters in this game.

273
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:19,760
Because this isn't a battle.

274
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:21,780
It's an Alto war.

275
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:25,220
It's your own fault for forgetting that.

276
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:32,020
What the hell is she still doing up there?

277
00:17:32,300 --> 00:17:34,440
Just looking at her pisses me off!

278
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:36,758
Hey, someone take care of that brat!

279
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,340
Right, on it, sir!

280
00:17:38,620 --> 00:17:40,080
Let's go! Yeah!

281
00:17:40,420 --> 00:17:42,800
Otama, hurry! Do it now!

282
00:17:43,820 --> 00:17:47,240
Hey, all my friends, you hate giving Tang!

283
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:50,357
I need to ask you a favor!

284
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:53,220
Can you switch sides, please?

285
00:17:53,700 --> 00:17:56,620
Big bro, Lumi, and Mama Natsuka need you!

286
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:58,600
You've got to have some fun!

287
00:18:03,420 --> 00:18:05,280
Let's all work together!

288
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:07,500
And turn down Carter!

289
00:18:16,380 --> 00:18:17,997
The hell was that?

290
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:22,640
You think they'll listen to you just
because you ass nice, you dumb brat?

291
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:25,960
You're gonna pay for
putting it on my show!

292
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:31,500
Roger that, Master!

293
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:33,252
Your wish is my command!

294
00:18:33,480 --> 00:18:34,760
Take down Tidal!

295
00:18:35,300 --> 00:18:36,940
Now, let's start with you!

296
00:18:39,040 --> 00:18:40,520
Get off of me!

297
00:18:40,820 --> 00:18:42,702
What the hell is wrong with you?

298
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:46,657
What's wrong, General Briscola? Let's go!

299
00:18:46,740 --> 00:18:50,622
We're here to take out some traitors,
so let's stomp them already!

300
00:18:51,100 --> 00:18:51,980
All right!

301
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:54,259
I heard you loud and clear, Master!

302
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:57,337
Let's start out with
a Gorilla Punch Punch!

303
00:18:57,420 --> 00:18:58,655
Just for you, Master!

304
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:00,470
All right.

305
00:19:00,553 --> 00:19:02,497
Looks like Master's given the order.

306
00:19:02,580 --> 00:19:04,020
Gazelle Man! Difugo!

307
00:19:04,820 --> 00:19:06,720
It's time to join the fight!

308
00:19:09,540 --> 00:19:11,020
You see that, Master?

309
00:19:11,220 --> 00:19:12,400
I'm working hard!

310
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:14,677
Why are all the dipters trying to kill us?

311
00:19:14,760 --> 00:19:15,597
I don't know, man!

312
00:19:15,680 --> 00:19:16,510
Just run away!

313
00:19:17,980 --> 00:19:19,740
We're coming for you, Kaido!

314
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:21,140
Let's do this!

315
00:19:23,260 --> 00:19:25,100
Everyone follow me!

316
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:32,500
Gifters, lend me your strength!

317
00:19:32,760 --> 00:19:36,054
Let's fight for our wonderful
master with all we've got!

318
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:50,660
You're the best!

319
00:19:50,880 --> 00:19:51,840
Thank you, guys!

320
00:19:57,980 --> 00:19:58,860
Oh, Christ!

321
00:19:59,060 --> 00:20:00,060
He's all bloated!

322
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:01,417
I told you he was dead.

323
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:03,040
And I told you to shut up!

324
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:04,497
You're not helping at all!

325
00:20:04,580 --> 00:20:05,410
What do we do?

326
00:20:05,493 --> 00:20:07,892
Captain can help if you were here, but...

327
00:20:08,860 --> 00:20:09,700
Stop fighting.

328
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:11,468
We need to clear his lungs.

329
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:14,140
One, two, three!

330
00:20:19,220 --> 00:20:20,050
Booviceye.

331
00:20:34,020 --> 00:20:36,757
Well, if he wasn't dead, you
might have just killed him.

332
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:38,428
He's rubber, he'll be fine.

333
00:20:39,100 --> 00:20:41,020
Well, I hope he will at least.

334
00:20:45,060 --> 00:20:45,890
Okay.

335
00:20:46,740 --> 00:20:47,570
It's not okay!

336
00:20:47,980 --> 00:20:49,537
Got it, that rubber's burnt.

337
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:51,440
Captain, help us!

338
00:20:57,500 --> 00:21:00,080
He missed you! He missed you!

339
00:21:03,380 --> 00:21:06,262
But like kites, we rise
highest against the wind!

340
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:09,800
Minpo, great kite!

341
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:17,710
Excellent!

342
00:21:18,060 --> 00:21:21,440
Now if I can just find a place to land...

343
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:28,457
That was awful...

344
00:21:28,540 --> 00:21:31,577
We escaped from that
horrible place, but...

345
00:21:31,660 --> 00:21:33,220
What caused...

346
00:21:33,740 --> 00:21:36,117
What happened to the others? Do you...

347
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:38,494
Do you think they could still be alive?

348
00:21:44,660 --> 00:21:45,490
Kiku...

349
00:21:45,573 --> 00:21:46,403
Kine-man!

350
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:48,220
Everyone!

351
00:22:03,860 --> 00:22:04,900
Conney!

352
00:22:13,340 --> 00:22:16,580
I think you mean father,
don't you, Yamato?

353
00:22:17,320 --> 00:22:19,800
I'm here to finally cut ties with you!

354
00:22:20,940 --> 00:22:21,770
Hmm.

355
00:22:23,300 --> 00:22:25,940
Are you sure about that, son?

356
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:41,717
Don't make me laugh.

357
00:22:41,800 --> 00:22:43,940
You have nothing without me.

358
00:22:44,880 --> 00:22:47,060
Straw Hat is sunk into the sea.

359
00:22:49,240 --> 00:22:51,680
Odin's son suffered the same fate.

360
00:22:53,720 --> 00:22:55,600
If you have the will to fight,

361
00:22:55,820 --> 00:22:58,657
you should have protected
them while you had the chance.

362
00:22:58,740 --> 00:22:59,857
You've got it wrong.

363
00:22:59,940 --> 00:23:01,377
I don't need to protect them.

364
00:23:01,460 --> 00:23:03,417
They're both much stronger than you think.

365
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:09,740
I fight beside them as equals
and what happens after that?

366
00:23:10,380 --> 00:23:13,860
You think you're gonna break
free of this country of me!

367
00:23:15,520 --> 00:23:19,717
Luffy will show me the world you've
kept from me, but before I leave here.

368
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:22,506
I'm kicking you out of
this country understand

369
00:23:34,560 --> 00:23:37,260
I won't be going anywhere.

370
00:23:40,260 --> 00:23:42,700
The land of water is extraordinary.

371
00:23:43,260 --> 00:23:45,260
There's no place like it.

372
00:23:46,400 --> 00:23:50,080
You can't defeat me, and I'll never leave.

373
00:23:51,380 --> 00:23:55,160
So stay with me, and become
the Shogun of this country!

374
00:23:57,200 --> 00:23:58,820
I told you no!

375
00:23:59,180 --> 00:24:01,768
And I know I won't be
the one to defeat you.

376
00:24:01,940 --> 00:24:02,840
That's Luffy!

377
00:24:03,500 --> 00:24:06,740
Because he's the man Kozuki
Oden was waiting for!

378
00:24:09,100 --> 00:24:11,620
He'll return, stronger than ever!

379
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:14,700
All I have to do is
keep you busy till then!

380
00:24:16,360 --> 00:24:19,780
Don't expect me to go easy on you, Yamato!

381
00:24:22,500 --> 00:24:23,840
No mercy!
